name: Edit an exact context copy, review it and select it for a finite study
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY NO_COLOR NODE_OPTIONS
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_MODEL=openai-codex:gpt-5.5
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_edit.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: use sast
submit: options sast:scan
submit: set taskMode manual
submit: set tasks secret-scan
submit: scan batch
require-live-snap: 20 PLAN A STUDY | study
keys: Down Down Down Enter Up Enter
require-live-snap: 25 CONTEXT SUMMARY | original-context
expect: Alpha
expect: e edit
keys: e
require-live-snap: 20 EDIT CONTEXT COPY | editable-fields
ask: Are the copy name, overview, components and question answers discoverable, with an inactive-copy boundary and visible edit/review/back controls?
keys: Enter C-u
paste-file: @ART/overview.txt
require-live-snap: 20 Unicode α | multiline-edit
ask: Does the text field own the complete multiline Unicode paste while its controls distinguish editing, review and saving?
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 ▸ * System overview | staged-overview
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 CONTEXT SUMMARY | original-retained
keys: e Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Unicode α | draft-restored
resize: 160x48
live-snap: editor-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: editor-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: editor-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: editor-60x20
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 20 Unicode α | editor-40x12
expect-echo-within: 300 retained-context-draft
live-snap: tiny-draft
expect: retained-context-draft
ask: Across the six sizes, does the editor retain its exact text and cursor with complete controls, including editable typing at 40x12?
resize: 120x36
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 ▸ * System overview | staged-full-overview
keys: Down Down Down Down Down Down Down
require-live-snap: 20 ▸ Answer 1 · Who owns the input? | selected-question
keys: Enter
paste-file: @ART/answer.txt
keys: C-s
require-live-snap: 20 REVIEW CONTEXT CHANGES | reviewed-changes
expect: Application owner
expect: Before:
expect: After:
expect: Answer 1 · Who owns the input?
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_edit.py @TMP_TARGET @ART draft
ask: Does review show the actual old and new text and explain that saving creates an inactive copy, while the original and active context remain unchanged?
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 30 Edited copy saved | saved-copy
ask: Does a successful save return to context choice with a clear inspection step, without silently selecting it for a study or changing the active model?
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Operator overview | inspect-copy
keys: PgDn
require-live-snap: 20 Answer: Application owner | inspect-answer
keys: a
require-live-snap: 20 Context selected for this study | selected-copy
keys: L
require-live-snap: 30 Draft ready | finite-plan
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_edit.py @TMP_TARGET @ART planned
ask: Does the selected copy feed the fixed three-pass draft, with unchanged active context, original objects and source, and zero jobs or model requests?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME NO_COLOR=1 KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_MODEL=openai-codex:gpt-5.5
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
paste-file: @ART/resume-command.txt
keys: Enter
nav-mode:
keys: a
require-live-snap: 20 PLAN A STUDY | recovered-study
keys: Down Down Down Enter Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Operator overview | recovered-copy
keys: PgDn
require-live-snap: 20 Answer: Application owner | recovered-answer
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_edit.py @TMP_TARGET @ART resumed
ask: Does a fresh no-color process recover the same edited context and human answer for the saved plan, while keeping the original active model and all work unstarted?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
